{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>A wolf shall tear.</b> The strength of the wolf and its tearing is in the morning and evening, when light is diminished, as it says: וְחַדּוּ מִזְּאֵבֵי עֶרֶב (Habakkuk 1:8). So too was the case with Benjamin: his kingship was at the dawn of his brothers' kingship, in the days of Saul, and after, the loss of his kingship in the days of Mordecai and Esther — for indeed the kingship of the Second Temple was but a moment, and with subjection upon the majority."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:35:27.769856876Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}